Text: INTRODUCTION According to The National Institute on Deafness, one in thousand infants is born deaf. An additional one to six per thousand are born with hearing loss at different levels [1]. Sign language is commonly used by Deaf and Hard-of- Hearing (DHH) persons to communicate via hand gestures. An automatic sign language recognizer enables an ASL user to translate the sign language to written text or speech, allowing them to communicate with people who are not familiar with ASL.

